      "notes": "Re-read from the 2.1.283 /model picker on 2026-09-26: Default (recommended), Opus 5.5, Fable 5.1, Sonnet 5, Haiku 4.5, then older versions (Opus 5, Fable 5, Opus 4.8, 4.7, 4.6, Sonnet 4.6). Its Opus 5.5 row is the 200K `opus`, and no row offers 1M any more: `opus[1m]` is reachable only through `claude --model opus[1m]` or `/model opus[1m]`, which saves it as the default. The catalog keeps `opus[1m]` as the default row and lists `opus` as its hidden twin, so the menu shows one Opus 5.5 row with a 200K/1M Context Window choice and a session on either size can change its effort (user decision 2026-09-26). The older versions are not listed. Quick picker cards use the full versioned labels (no quickPickerLabel): the user asked that Claude models always show their version in the quick picker and the composer."
    },
